  "summary": "The identified studies directly apply Boosted Decision-Tree Ensembles to the topic of estimating battery remaining life. The reported performance metrics vary across datasets, with AUROC values reaching 0.88 on GridWatch [V0087] and accuracy reported at 0.74 on CellLife [V0085]. Other evaluations report an MAE of 0.81 on ToxiBench [V0086] and an F1 score of 0.6 on ProtMap [V0088]. While several candidate documents mention the application of boosted decision-tree ensembles to battery remaining life in their discussion of prior work, they are excluded from the primary ranking as they apply different methods such as Self-Attention Encoder Models [V0078, V0080] or Representation Learning [V0095, V0094] to the same topic, or apply the method to different topics entirely [V0038, V0205].",
